  "id": "COMPOUND:15029 - PROTEIN:5817",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 12,13-Dihydroxybakuchiol and HepG2 through a series of target interactions. The compound is linked to Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is targeted by multiple agents, including 4-Fluorobenzoic acid, tridec-2-ynyl ester and Petroraspailyne B1. All these targets ultimately interact with HepG2, indicating a possible pathway where 12,13-Dihydroxybakuchiol may influence HepG2 through the modulation of Microtubule-associated protein 1B. The evidence suggests that the compound may act as a modulator of this protein, which in turn affects HepG2 through a mechanism that is not fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Microtubule-associated protein 1B as a potential mediator in the interaction between 12,13-Dihydroxybakuchiol and HepG2, though further investigation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism of action.",
